[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a one-line change, but it's a session-lifetime change, so I want a yes before I edit rather than after.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m is [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m, read by [38;5;153mserver.js[39m as the session expiry. Going to 480 means an idle or
  abandoned session — a shared machine, a stolen laptop, a hijacked session token — stays usable for a full working day
  instead of half an hour. That's a 16x widening of the window for session-hijack and unattended-access, and it applies
  to every user, not just the case that prompted the request.

  Nothing else in the repo depends on the value, so the edit itself is trivial and safe to make.

